From fca4aff95764f3353c125fe7c94d18bf71bd4b75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:49:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: imx471 TEMP DIAG (0084) -- powered scan on CCI1 master
 1

Re-adds an in-driver address scan, but for the first time on the bus the
vendor actually assigns to the front camera.

Every previous scan is disqualified:

  0070  master 0, wrong CCI clock, VANA inverted   -> sensor unpowered
  0075  master 0, clock fixed, VANA inverted       -> sensor unpowered
  0079  master 0, VANA fixed                       -> wrong bus entirely

0079 was run correctly but pointed at CCI1 master 0, which patch 0083
established is the GC5035 macro camera's bus. The 0x50/0x58 that answered
throughout belong to the GC5035's EEPROM, not the front module.

This scan runs on master 1 with VANA polarity correct (0077), the vendor
power sequence VANA->VDIG->VIO->MCLK->RESET (0082), and a 400kHz bus
(0078/0083), after reset release and the 50-60ms settle.

The addresses that matter are 0x54 and 0x5c: the front module's own
EEPROM, fed from the same VIO/VDIG/VANA this driver now sequences and
carried on the same flex as the image sensor. Three outcomes:

  0x54/0x5c ACK, 0x1a silent  the module is present and powered, and the
                              image sensor specifically does not answer.
                              First correctly-targeted evidence for a
                              sensor-level fault.

  0x1a ACKs                   solved.

  nothing ACKs                the fault is upstream of the module --
                              rails, flex seating or the bus itself --
                              and is not sensor-specific.

Temporary. Revert once the question is settled.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
index b960737ca..55b267e21 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
@@ -593,6 +593,43 @@ static int imx471_power_on(struct device *dev)
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(sensor->reset_gpio, 0);
 	usleep_range(50000, 60000);
 
+	/*
+	 * TEMP DIAGNOSTIC (0084, revert once resolved).
+	 *
+	 * Scan this adapter while the part is genuinely powered and out of
+	 * reset. This is the first time such a scan runs on the bus the vendor
+	 * actually assigns the front camera to (CCI1 master 1, patch 0083),
+	 * with correct VANA polarity (0077) and the vendor power sequence
+	 * (0082). Every earlier scan (0070, 0075, 0079) ran on master 0 --
+	 * the GC5035 macro camera's bus -- and/or with the sensor unpowered.
+	 *
+	 * What matters is 0x54/0x5c. Those are the front module's OWN EEPROM,
+	 * which shares this module's VIO/VDIG/VANA rails and sits on the same
+	 * flex. If they answer and 0x1a stays silent, the module is present
+	 * and powered while its image sensor specifically is not responding.
+	 * If nothing at all answers, the fault is upstream of the module.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct i2c_client *client = to_i2c_client(dev);
+		struct i2c_adapter *adap = client->adapter;
+		int addr, found = 0;
+
+		dev_info(dev, "imx471 DIAG(0084): powered scan of %s\n",
+			 adap->name);
+		for (addr = 0x08; addr <= 0x77; addr++) {
+			union i2c_smbus_data data;
+
+			if (i2c_smbus_xfer(adap, addr, 0, I2C_SMBUS_READ, 0,
+					   I2C_SMBUS_BYTE, &data) >= 0) {
+				dev_info(dev, "imx471 DIAG(0084): 0x%02x ACKED\n",
+					 addr);
+				found++;
+			}
+		}
+		dev_info(dev, "imx471 DIAG(0084): scan done, %d device(s)\n",
+			 found);
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 
